{"url": "https://www.cb.cityu.edu.hk/en/pg/research-degree-programmes/introduction", "final_url": "https://www.cb.cityu.edu.hk/en/pg/research-degree-programmes/introduction", "status": 200, "method": "http", "fetched": "2026-11-18", "text": "Research Degree Programmes : Introduction | CityUHK Postgraduate Admissions\nPostgraduate Admissions \u7814\u7a76\u751f\u8ab2\u7a0b\u62db\u751f\nHome\nAbout CityUHK\nOverview\nIntroduction\nWhy CityUHK\nStudents and Alumni Sharing\nFacilities & Supports\nResearch Degree Programmes\nOverview\nIntroduction\nResearch Areas\nEntrance Requirements\nSteps & Procedures\nScholarships, Financial Aid & Fees\nHK PhD Fellowship Scheme\nApply Now\nProfessional Doctorate Programmes\nOverview\nIntroduction\nProgramme List\nSteps & Procedures\nApply Now\nMaster's Programmes\nOverview\nIntroduction\nProgramme List\nEntrance Requirements\nSteps & Procedures\nFAQs\nApply Now\nHong Kong Future Talents Scholarship Scheme for Advanced Studies (FTSS)\nLatest Updates\nVisiting\nOverview\nVisiting Research Students\nVisiting Postgraduate Students\nApply Now\nOverview\nResearch Degree Programmes\nProfessional Doctorate Programmes\nMaster's Programmes\nNews and Events\nInformation Session\nCityUHK NewsCentre\nQuick Links\nChow Yei Ching School of Graduate Studies\nProgramme Search\nHong Kong Future Talents Scholarship Scheme for Advanced Studies for Local Students (Master's)\nHK PhD Fellowship Scheme\nOther Scholarship\nContact Us\nRegistered Applicants' Login\n\u7e41\nSearch\nResearch Degree Programmes\nPrevious\nNext\nSubmenu : RPg\nIntroduction\nResearch Areas\nEntrance Requirements\nSteps & Procedures\nScholarships, Financial Aid & Fees\nHK PhD Fellowship Scheme\nApply Now\nCityUHK offers two types of research degree programmes: Master of Philosophy (MPhil) and Doctor of Philosophy (PhD). MPhil and PhD programmes are offered in all Colleges and Schools in a wide range of strategic areas to reflect the University\u2019s strengths and to suit individuals\u2019 research interests. These programmes consist of both coursework and independent research studies culminating in the submission of a thesis.\nCityUHK provides a modern teaching and learning environment with the latest educational technology to support high-quality teaching and research activities. We offer studentships, scholarships, conference grants and other financial assistance so that students can engage in more academic exchange activities that are beneficial and related to their research studies. Through collaboration with scholars in different regions, students can bring their research skills to new levels.\nA wide range of facilities and services are provided to support students\u2019 studies and recreational activities. Student residence halls are also available on campus to provide students with residential accommodation and to offer an avenue for academic and cultural exchange.\nFinancial Assistance\nMore details\nAround 80% of research students are non-local and represent a wide range of nationalities from 50+ countries\nResearch Achievements\nMore details\nTop-Notch Scholars\nProf. WAN Tze-Kin Alan\nProf. MA Yue\nProf. FENG Shien Ping\nProf. CHEN Yangyang\nProf. HUI Shu Yuen Ron\nProf. CHEN Youhua Frank\nProf. HUANG Yi-hui\nProf. FAN Ruiping\nProf. ZHANG Qingfu\nProf. ZHOU Shuhua\nProf. LUK Kwai Man\nProf. HUANG Yu\nProf. David X W LOU\nProf. HORTON Benjamin\nProf. LO Kam Wing Kenneth\nProf. CHAN Ngai Hang\nProf. LI Wen Jung\nProf. YANG Yong\nProf. Andrey ROGACH\nProf. FENG Gang Gary\nProf. CHEN Guanrong\nProf. Kalok CHAN\nProf. CHAN Chi Hou\nProf. LI Ying\nProf. YIP Hin Lap\nProf. Espen AARSETH\nProf. CHEN Fu-Rong\nProf. CHI Yun\nProf. YANG M\nProf. LEUNG Mei Yee Kenneth\nProf. YUAN Zhiguo\nProf. BAO Wei\nProf. HIBIKI Takashi\nProf. GUO Pengfei\nProf. YUNG Wing Ho\nProf. FANG Yuguang\nProf. WU Dapeng\nProf. GUO Zaiping\nProf. LI Qiusheng\nProf. WANG Wenxiong\nProf. ZHANG Yong\nProf. LIU Hongyu\nProf. LEE Duu-Jong\nProf. MA Wei-Ying\nProf. REN Yang\nProf. LEUNG Kwok Wa\nProf. WANG Xin\nProf. ZENG Xiaocheng\nProf. ZHANG Shujun\nProf. Josep POU\nProf. THOMPSON Mark Richard\nProf. TSAI Din-ping\nProf. SUN Dong\nProf. SCHILLER Niels O.\nProf. TAN Siew Chong\nProf. LU Jane\nProf. YUEN Kwok Kit Richard\nProf. DONG Zhao Yang\nProf. HO Johnny Chung Yin\nProf. GUO Yongxin\nProf. LEUNG Kwok Hi Michael\nProf. WANG Xun-Li\nProf. Stella W. PANG\nProf. LIEW Kim Meow\nProf. KIM Sungmoon\nProf. Vanessa Rosemary Duke BARRS\nProf. KAI Ji-jung\nProf. ZHU Yuntian\nMORE SCHOLARS\nProgramme Structure\nTo be eligible to be awarded a MPhil/PhD degree, students are required to complete the following coursework requirements and to submit a thesis.\nMPhil: 7 credit units (including at least 2 credit units of research methodology and ethics course at postgraduate level);\nPhD: 14 credit units (including at least 9 credit units of core courses and at least 2 credit units of research methodology and ethics course at postgraduate level)\nand\n1 credit unit compulsory course: Teaching Students: First Steps (SG8001)\nand\nTraining on Research Integrity (CITI Programme).\nIndividual Departments and Schools may stipulate higher credit unit requirements.\nAbout CityUHK\nIntroduction\nWhy CityUHK\nStudents and Alumni Sharing\nFacilities & Supports\nResearch Degree Programmes\nIntroduction\nResearch Areas\nEntrance Requirements\nSteps & Procedures\nScholarships, Financial Aid & Fees\nHK PhD Fellowship Scheme\nApply Now\nProfessional Doctorate Programmes\nIntroduction\nProgramme List\nSteps & Procedures\nApply Now\nMaster's Programmes\nIntroduction\nProgramme List\nEntrance Requirements\nSteps & Procedures\nFAQs\nApply Now\nHong Kong Future Talents Scholarship Scheme for Advanced Studies (FTSS)\nLatest Updates\nVisiting\nVisiting Research Students\nVisiting Postgraduate Students\nApply Now\nResearch Degree Programmes\nProfessional Doctorate Programmes\nMaster's Programmes\nNews and Events\nInformation Session\nCityUHK NewsCentre\nContact Us\nPr